      {
        "id": "0b140000-0000-4000-8000-000000000025",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Staff follow the allergy action plan signed by your child's doctor or nurse. In outline:",
        "alignment": "left"
      },
      {
        "id": "0b140000-0000-4000-8000-000000000026",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "A mild or moderate reaction may show as swollen lips, face or eyes, an itchy or tingling mouth, hives or an itchy rash, tummy pain or vomiting, or a sudden change in behaviour. Staff stay with your child, call for help, give the antihistamine named in the plan, and call you.",
        "runs": [
          {
            "text": "A mild or moderate reaction",
            "bold": true
          },
          {
            "text": " may show as swollen lips, face or eyes, an itchy or tingling mouth, hives or an itchy rash, tummy pain or vomiting, or a sudden change in behaviour. Staff stay with your child, call for help, give the antihistamine named in the plan, and call you."
          }
        ],
        "alignment": "left"
      },
      {
        "id": "0b140000-0000-4000-8000-000000000027",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Anaphylaxis is a reaction that affects the airway, breathing or consciousness: a persistent cough, a hoarse voice, difficulty swallowing or a swollen tongue; difficult or noisy breathing or wheezing; or feeling faint, going pale or floppy, becoming suddenly sleepy or collapsing.",
        "runs": [
          {
            "text": "Anaphylaxis",
            "bold": true
          },
          {
            "text": " is a reaction that affects the airway, breathing or consciousness: a persistent cough, a hoarse voice, difficulty swallowing or a swollen tongue; difficult or noisy breathing or wheezing; or feeling faint, going pale or floppy, becoming suddenly sleepy or collapsing."
          }
        ],
        "alignment": "left"
      },
      {
        "id": "0b140000-0000-4000-8000-000000000028",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "If any of these signs appear, staff will:",
        "runs": [
          {
            "text": "If any of these signs appear,",
            "bold": true
          },
          {
            "text": " staff will:"
          }
        ],
        "alignment": "left"
      },
      {
        "id": "0b140000-0000-4000-8000-000000000029",
        "type": "numbered_list",
        "items": [
          "Lie your child down with their legs raised, or let them sit up if breathing is difficult. They will not stand or walk.",
          "Use the adrenaline auto-injector without delay.",
          "Dial 999, ask for an ambulance and say \"anaphylaxis\".",
          "Call you.",
          "Give a second auto-injector after 5 minutes if your child is no better."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "0b140000-0000-4000-8000-000000000030",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "If in doubt, staff give adrenaline. A child with asthma who suddenly has difficulty breathing is treated as having anaphylaxis.",
        "runs": [
          {
            "text": "If in doubt, staff give adrenaline.",
            "bold": true
          },
          {
            "text": " A child with asthma who suddenly has difficulty breathing is treated as having anaphylaxis."
          }
        ],
        "alignment": "left"
      },
